# LIQUID-08 — Avoid unnecessary JSON serialization

## Rationale

Using `| json` on large objects (full `product`, `collection`, `cart`) is
CPU-intensive, bloats HTML, slows parse time, and sends data the client never
uses.

## How to check

```bash
bun "<skill-dir>/scripts/cli.ts" check liquid-performance <file>
```

Flags large object `| json` usage (review whether the serialized object is minimal).

## How to fix

Use data attributes for individual fields, or build a minimal JSON object with
only the properties JavaScript needs.

## Examples

### Bad

```liquid
<div class="product-card" data-product="{{ product | json }}">
  <span class="current-price">{{ product.price | money }}</span>
</div>
```

### Good

```liquid
<div class="product-card"
     data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
     data-product-price-cents="{{ product.price }}">
  <span class="current-price">{{ product.price | money }}</span>
</div>
```

Or serialize only variant id → price pairs needed for client updates.
